    {
      "start": 0.940000000000003,
      "end": 5.68,
      "text": "Talk about the ultimate breakup. Europe and Africa have been splitting apart from the",
      "avg_logprob": -0.19166511535644531,
      "no_speech_prob": 0.10748270899057388,
      "compression_ratio": 1.6296296296296295
    },
    {
      "start": 5.68,
      "end": 11.34,
      "text": "American continents for millions of years. At a rate of approximately 2.5 centimeters per",
      "avg_logprob": -0.19166511535644531,
      "no_speech_prob": 0.10748270899057388,
      "compression_ratio": 1.6296296296296295
    },
    {
      "start": 11.34,
      "end": 15.9,
      "text": "year, the continents are moving about as fast as our fingernails grow, and as they continue",
      "avg_logprob": -0.19166511535644531,
      "no_speech_prob": 0.10748270899057388,
      "compression_ratio": 1.6296296296296295
    },
    {
      "start": 15.9,
      "end": 20.5,
      "text": "to split, the rift between them. Otherwise known as the Atlantic Ocean, we'll get even",
      "avg_logprob": -0.19166511535644531,
      "no_speech_prob": 0.10748270899057388,
      "compression_ratio": 1.6296296296296295
    },
    {
      "start": 20.5,
      "end": 26.44,
      "text": "wider. And all this drama is leaving behind a major scar. An underwater valley called",
      "avg_logprob": -0.19166511535644531,
      "no_speech_prob": 0.10748270899057388,
      "compression_ratio": 1.6296296296296295
    },
    {
      "start": 26.44,
      "end": 31.06,
      "text": "the mid-Atlantic ridge, which tears more and more as the continents slowly move apart.",
      "avg_logprob": -0.24690784917813596,
      "no_speech_prob": 0.015747329220175743,
      "compression_ratio": 1.6115384615384616
    },
    {
      "start": 31.42,
      "end": 36.64,
      "text": "Looking back on the continental relationship, puts us in mere 300 million years ago, when",
      "avg_logprob": -0.24690784917813596,
      "no_speech_prob": 0.015747329220175743,
      "compression_ratio": 1.6115384615384616
    },
    {
      "start": 36.64,
      "end": 42.12,
      "text": "Africa, Europe, the Americas, and all the other continents for one big landmass, the",
      "avg_logprob": -0.24690784917813596,
      "no_speech_prob": 0.015747329220175743,
      "compression_ratio": 1.6115384615384616
    },
    {
      "start": 42.12,
      "end": 44.42,
      "text": "famed supercontinent, Pangaea.",
      "avg_logprob": -0.24690784917813596,
      "no_speech_prob": 0.015747329220175743,
      "compression_ratio": 1.6115384615384616
    },
    {
      "start": 44.92,
      "end": 50.1,
      "text": "Due to the constant churning of magma underneath the Earth's crust, they all split up and",
      "avg_logprob": -0.24690784917813596,
      "no_speech_prob": 0.015747329220175743,
      "compression_ratio": 1.6115384615384616
    },
    {
      "start": 50.1,
      "end": 51.62,
      "text": "moved to their modern day positions.",
      "avg_logprob": -0.24690784917813596,
      "no_speech_prob": 0.015747329220175743,
      "compression_ratio": 1.6115384615384616
    },
    {
      "start": 51.62,
      "end": 56.64,
      "text": "But if destiny and the form of magma and tectonic plates has anything to say about it,",
      "avg_logprob": -0.24419385931465062,
      "no_speech_prob": 0.2458738535642624,
      "compression_ratio": 1.6772727272727272
    },
    {
      "start": 56.88,
      "end": 60.74,
      "text": "the continents might have a chance of getting back together, but how will these stubborn",
      "avg_logprob": -0.24419385931465062,
      "no_speech_prob": 0.2458738535642624,
      "compression_ratio": 1.6772727272727272
    },
    {
      "start": 60.74,
      "end": 61.96,
      "text": "continents kiss and make up?",
      "avg_logprob": -0.24419385931465062,
      "no_speech_prob": 0.2458738535642624,
      "compression_ratio": 1.6772727272727272
    },
    {
      "start": 62.34,
      "end": 66.64,
      "text": "Scientists believe the plates will shift, causing the continents to rearrange and get back",
      "avg_logprob": -0.24419385931465062,
      "no_speech_prob": 0.2458738535642624,
      "compression_ratio": 1.6772727272727272
    },
    {
      "start": 66.64,
      "end": 67.18,
      "text": "together.",
      "avg_logprob": -0.24419385931465062,
      "no_speech_prob": 0.2458738535642624,
      "compression_ratio": 1.6772727272727272
    },
    {
